==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es|-}}

# {{uncountable}} The property of being [[thick]] (in dimension).
# {{uncountable}} A measure of how thick (in dimension) something is.
#: ''The '''thickness''' of the Earth's crust is varies from two to 70 kilometres.''
# {{countable}} A layer.
#: ''We upholstered the seat with three '''thicknesses''' of cloth to make it more comfortable to sit on.''
# {{uncountable}} The quality of being thick (in consistency).
#: ''Whip the cream until it reaches a good '''thickness'''.''
# {{uncountable|informal}} The property of being thick (slow to understand).

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|the property of being thick in dimension}} [[fatness]]
* {{sense|measure}} [[depth]]
* {{sense|layer}} [[layer]], [[stratum]]
* {{sense|in consistency}} [[density]], [[viscosity]]
* {{sense|property of being stupid}} [[denseness]], [[slowness]], [[stupidity]], [[thickheadedness]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|in consistency}} [[fluidity]], [[liquidity]], [[runniness]], [[thinness]], [[wateriness]]
* {{sense|property of being stupid}} mental [[acuity]], mental [[agility]], [[quick-wittedness]], [[sharpness]]

